    "rich_text_UQEXFr": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_Hby3Ph": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "enlarge_text": false,
            "text": "<p>For twenty-five years, I was a primary school teacher, and I loved every single one of them.</p><p>Every school holiday, my husband and I would drive up to Wasaga Beach — and the moment those sandy shores came into view, something in me would exhale.</p><p>Eight years ago, after my last class, a small boutique came up for lease not far from that same beach.</p><p>My husband, Tom, looked at me across the kitchen table and didn't say a word.</p><p>He didn't have to.</p><p>I'd spent twenty-five years helping children discover their confidence. Now, I wanted to help women rediscover theirs.</p><p>So we made the move.</p><p>That same year, I opened the doors of Margaret's Wasaga Beach for the very first time.</p><p>Now I'm sixty-four, and it's time to close this chapter.</p><p>Not because something went wrong.</p><p>Because something went beautifully right — and I'm wise enough to know when a story has reached its ending.</p><p>This is my favourite sale.</p><p>Every piece I've ever chosen for this boutique was chosen with one woman in mind — the real woman, not the one on the hanger.</p><p>The woman who deserves to feel beautiful.<br/>The woman who has spent years putting everyone else first.<br/>The woman who sometimes just needs to find one piece that makes her feel like herself again.</p><p>That hasn't changed.</p><p>Everything must go, at the lowest prices I've ever offered.</p><p>So come in, take your time, and find something that makes you stop.</p><p>Trust that feeling.</p><p>I built this little place around exactly that moment.</p><p>With love,</p><p>Margaret Anderson ❤️</p><p>Margaret's Wasaga Beach</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_Hby3Ph"
      ],
